# Sakina Sacred Use License (Draft)

Version 0.1 — May 2026
Status: Draft, pending solicitor review.

This license is supplementary to the per-response presentation
contracts emitted in `_sakina_meta.presentation_contract` and
`_sakina_meta.llm_directives` on every tool call. The contract
binds the agent's *output*; this license binds the human or
organisation distributing or integrating with this software.

By installing, deploying, or integrating with the Sakina Islamic
Knowledge MCP Server (the "Software"), you agree to the terms below.
If you cannot agree, do not install it.

---

## 1. The content

The Software ships with curated Islamic content originating from
Sakina (asksakina.com): the 99 Names of Allah with reflections, a
444-entry du'a corpus with hadith citations and grading, and Quranic
verses fetched at runtime from a public upstream (alquran.cloud, with
Tanzil-derived Arabic and conventional translations). All embedded
content has been reviewed through the project's structured
specialist-AI review chain (the "Gems") for theological accuracy,
pastoral safety, and inclusivity across mainstream Sunni schools. This
structured AI review is not performed by human scholars and is not a
substitute for a qualified scholar.

The Sakina team (the "Project") is the rights holder for the
curated content embedded in the Software. The Project also asserts a
duty of care over how that content is presented, downstream of the
agent boundary.

## 2. Permitted uses

You may, at no cost:

- Install the Software locally and connect it to AI agents you control
  (Claude Desktop, VS Code, custom agents) for personal or
  educational use.
- Run the Software as a private instance for your team, organisation,
  or community, including behind authentication.
- Quote, extract, or display the Software's responses verbatim in
  applications you build, **provided you preserve the
  `_sakina_meta` envelope's disclaimer, presentation contract, and
  source attribution**.
- Cite the Software as a source of Islamic content with the URL
  `https://www.asksakina.com` and the project name "Sakina".
- Translate, transcribe, or audio-render the verbatim Arabic text
  contained in responses for non-commercial educational purposes.
- Fork the Software for the purpose of submitting pull requests
  back to the upstream repository.

## 3. Prohibited uses

You may not, under any circumstances:

- Modify, paraphrase, or selectively quote the Arabic text of
  Quranic verses or the matn (text) of any hadith returned by the
  Software. Quranic and prophetic text must be reproduced verbatim.
- Strip the hadith grading from any hadith you display. Grading is
  part of the text, not optional metadata.
- Strip or alter the surah:ayah reference of any Quranic verse you
  display.
- Strip the disclaimer from any user-facing surface that uses
  Software-sourced content.
- Use the unicode honorific symbol after the Prophet Muhammad's name
  ("ﷺ", U+FDFA) in any surface where Software-sourced content is
  displayed. The spelt-out form "(peace be upon him)" must be used
  instead, in deference to a stated editorial choice of the Project.
- Repackage Software responses as a fatwa, religious ruling, or
  authoritative scholarly opinion. The Software is reference content,
  not a substitute for a qualified local scholar.
- Use the Software to train AI models that misrepresent Islam, or
  to generate content that promotes hatred, harm, or extremism.
- Use the Software's name "Sakina" or the domain "asksakina.com"
  in your product's name, logo, or marketing in a way that implies
  the Project endorses your application without written permission.
- Strip, hide, or de-emphasise the crisis-resource block when it
  appears in a response. The block is the project's safety contract;
  agents that suppress it are operating in violation of this license.

## 4. Attribution

If you display Software-sourced content in a user-facing application,
please credit Sakina:

> Islamic content provided by Sakina (asksakina.com).

A discreet credit on a colophon page or near the relevant content
section is sufficient. There is no requirement to credit on every
individual quote.

## 5. Distribution of the Software itself

The Software code is licensed for redistribution provided you:

- Retain this LICENSE file unmodified.
- Retain the README and the per-response presentation contracts.
- Do not strip or replace the `_sakina_meta` envelope from
  responses your fork emits.
- Make a reasonable effort to track upstream releases. Distributing
  a stale fork that misses critical safety or grading corrections
  could harm users.

## 6. No warranty

The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The
Project makes a good-faith effort to ensure accuracy, but Islamic
scholarship is a vast and contested field. Always consult a
qualified local scholar for matters of personal religious obligation.

The Project shall not be liable for damages arising from the use of
the Software, including (without limitation) damages from agent
misrepresentation of returned content.

## 7. Termination

If you materially violate this license — by paraphrasing Quranic
text, dropping hadith grading, suppressing the crisis-resource
block, or repackaging the Software's content as a fatwa — your
permission to use the Software terminates automatically. The
Project may issue a public notice of withdrawal in the MCP
registries and may revoke access to any hosted instance.

You may resume use after demonstrating good-faith remediation.
The Project's preference is always remediation over confrontation;
please reach out at the contact below.

---

## Contact

For licensing questions, takedown requests, or to discuss commercial
or institutional use that doesn't fit the model above, contact:

- Web: https://www.asksakina.com
- Issues: https://github.com/yserrag/asksakina-mcp/issues

---

## A note on tone

This license is itself an act of dawah (an invitation to the way of
Allah). The rules above are not a wall — they are the architecture
that lets Islamic content reach AI agents intact. We ask that you
honour them in the same spirit they were drafted: with care for the
sacred and respect for the thirty thousand human beings already
quietly using Sakina each month.

May Allah accept this work and use it for good.

---

> **Note to integrators:** the per-response `_sakina_meta` envelope
> contains a `presentation_contract` field that is your operational
> reference. This LICENSE governs distribution and integration; the
> contract governs presentation. Both apply.
